# Check every text file out with LF line endings, on Windows too (16 Nov: a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true got
# CRLF files, and the docs parsers, the README checks and npm run judge read each line with its trailing \r).
* text=auto eol=lf
# Kept byte for byte: the ISO 20022 schema is stored with CRLF as published.
test/fixtures/iso20022/*.xsd -text
# Binary, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.sqlite binary
# The release tarball (`git archive` in release.yml) leaves out the screenshots, recordings and films under docs/: the
# build and the tests do not need them, and they made the tarball 238 MB (sizes in docs/releasing.md). They stay in git
# and on GitHub. Kept: every image the code or a test reads, found by running the whole test suite on the archive
# (19 Nov): the README's images (a test lists docs/assets/readme/), the media and screens folders with the READMEs that
# describe them, the images the site's pages embed, the submission form's screenshots, and each file a doc links to
# (the relative-link test) or the code opens.
docs/**/*.mp4 export-ignore
docs/**/*.webm export-ignore
docs/**/*.mov export-ignore
docs/**/*.gif export-ignore
docs/**/*.png export-ignore
docs/**/*.jpg export-ignore
